    "reason": "While '名称' (meishou) translates to 'name' or 'title' and is used for formal or official names (e.g., company names, product names), it is a narrower term than the general English 'name'. For a general language learner, '名前' (namae) is the standard, most common, and natural translation for 'name', especially when referring to personal names or general objects. Using '名称' for the broad concept of 'name' would be less natural and potentially confusing for learners.",
